   "content": "# Hackathon radar · Tue Oct 27\n\n**Three things changed since yesterday.** All names, counts and dates here are example data from fixtures, not real events.\n\n- **Rules:** the example rules page now requires a public repository with a visible open-source licence. Ours has one; the licence file must stay at the repo root.\n- **Pace:** 3 new submissions in the Personal AI track (example data); the deadline is Nov 15, 10:00 UTC.\n- **Competitor:** Example Project A (Personal AI track) is a chat agent that drafts actions for approval: the same approval idea, one chat app, no crew, no learning.\n\n## Who else is building a personal agent\n\n| project | track | what it does | overlap with Nimbus |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Example Project A | Personal AI | chat agent that asks before each action | approvals only |\n| Example Project B | Apps & Agents | shared to-do lists | none |\n| Example Project C | Apps & Agents | recurring reminders | none |\n\n## Say differently\n\nLead with the crew and the learning loop, not \"an agent with approvals\": approvals are table stakes now.\n\n*Source news (example): cached input is billed at a lower rate; our role prompts are a stable prefix for exactly this.*",
